  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday) Issued at 1200 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will continue to slowly drift back towards the \nsoutheast thus rain chances will eventually come to an end by \nTuesday. Temperatures will continue to increase a little more each \nday into next week before peaking by late week. Air temperatures \nduring this stretch are forecast to reach the 100-102 degree range \nfor many areas every day. These higher temperatures combined with \nthe humidity may produce Heat Advisory criteria (108 degrees or \nhigher) for areas mainly east of I-37/I-35. The hot and mainly dry \nweather looks to stick around heading into next weekend. Humidity \nvalues should be a touch lower along with high temps mainly in the \nupper 90s so we should stay just shy of heat advisory criteria \nduring this stretch however it will still continue to be quite hot \nacross the area. Continue to check back for updates and remember to \npractice safe heat safety.",
